CODEGEN.md §5.6, DECISIONS 307, 350: a discriminant read through a ref is decided at build time, but not through an optional field of the record itself: the ref ev may be absent, so the payload's discriminant is optional, which no loader reads: DependentType at the field, in go types and data mode alike.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A kind.
enum K { one, two }

/// An event.
record Ev {
  /// Its kind.
  k: K
}

/// The events.
let evs: table Ev = { x { k: one } }

/// A payload.
type P(e: Ev) = match e.k { one => Int, two => String }

/// A thing.
record Thing {
  /// Its event, maybe.
  ev: ref evs?
  /// Its payload.
  p: P(ev)?
}

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a", mode: types }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8019]  a/a.canon:23:3
  emit go in types mode cannot generate a dependent value decided through an optional, a record parameter, a ref into a `@reload` value or a ref into an enclosing record's table field; decide it by an enum field of the same record, or by a ref into a let that is not `@reload`

